@defgroup micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api C++ API
@brief How to write the tests.

@details
All the definitions are in the `micro_os_plus::micro_test_plus`
namespace, which the examples shorten with an alias:

@code{.cpp}
#include <micro-os-plus/micro-test-plus.h>

namespace mt = micro_os_plus::micro_test_plus;
@endcode

The topics follow the structure of a test program:
- the runner, which starts and ends the session;
- the suites, which group the test cases;
- the test cases, which hold the checks;
- the checks: the expectations, which are counted, and the requirements,
  which also stop the test case when they fail;
- the conditions of the checks: the function comparators, the logical
  functions, and the exception checks;
- the string utilities;
- the customisation, for the application types and comparators;
- the deprecated definitions, kept for the existing tests.
